ccowsay
=======
ccowsay displays a message in a speech or thought bubble and renders
an ASCII cow template below it.

Usage:

    ccowsay [options] <message>

With no message, read standard input.

Options:

    -h, --help           Show this help
    -l, --list           List available cows
    -f, --file <cow>     Select cow template
    -c, --cow <cow>      Alias for -f
    -e, --eyes <xx>      Set two eye characters
    -T, --tongue <xx>    Set two tongue characters
    -t, --thought        Render a thought bubble
    -n, --no-wrap        Preserve input lines
    -W, --wrap <cols>    Wrap message at column count
    -b -d -g -p -s -w -y Face modes

Cow templates are plain text files. The renderer replaces $eyes,
$tongue, and $thoughts while printing them.

Cow path: CCOWSAY_COWPATH, then COWPATH, then the compiled default cow
directory.

Examples:

```console
$ ccowsay Hello ALT Linux
 _________________
< Hello ALT Linux >
 -----------------
        \   ^__^
         \  (oo)\_______
            (__)\       )\/\
                ||----w |
                ||     ||
```

```console
$ CCOWSAY_COWPATH=./cows ccowsay -f tux "Linux is here"
 _______________
< Linux is here >
 ---------------
   \
    \
        .--.
       |o_o |
       |:_/ |
      //   \ \
     (|     | )
    /'\_   _/`\
    \___)=(___/
```

```console
$ CCOWSAY_COWPATH=./cows ccowsay -t -e "bd" -f small "I am thinking"
 _______________
( I am thinking )
 ---------------
       o   ,__,
        o  (bd)____
           (__)    )\
              ||--|| *
```
